// MODELDEF MODEL FRAMES ARE NOT INHERITED. FindModelFrameRaw matches on
// `smff->type == ti` -- an exact class-POINTER compare with no walk up
// the hierarchy (engine source, src/r_data/models.cpp:1165). So the four
// base-class blocks above cover VR_Pistol and nothing else: VR_Pistol2
// through VR_Pistol6 get no model at all.
//
// Those five have no sprite either -- PSP1/BFP1/PLP1/RLP1 have no lumps
// anywhere in sprites/, which is the whole reason the block above exists.
// No sprite AND no model is an actor that renders NOTHING while staying
// solid, touchable and pickup-able. That is exactly the reported symptom:
// a weapon on the floor you cannot see and can still walk into.
//
// It matters more than it looks, because the numbered identities are the
// ONLY thing the world ever spawns for these families. An elite drop
// builds its class as GetMainhandClass() .. "2".."6"
// (RS_EliteDrop.zs:429) and the pedestal gap-fill does the same
// (RS_ClassGating.zs:370) -- the bare base class is spawned by the dev
// harness and by almost nothing else. So a VR_Dual_Pistol player saw
// every floor weapon as thin air while `netevent rs-panel-test` showed a
// perfectly visible one, which is about as misleading as a repro gets.
//
// If a seventh identity is ever added, it needs a block here too.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

